  "notes": [
    "Original inputs generated by the PR2 Rust writer acceptance example; exact input bytes are reproduced in integration tests.",
    "All three cases opened, saved, closed, reopened, saved and closed with normal exit. Basic and settings also have native DXF exports.",
    "Jw_cad normalizes an empty memo to CRLF, wraps arc starts, recomputes text baseline endpoints and appends internal setting TEXT records.",
    "Empty TEXT is retained by the Rust codec but removed on native save. Nonempty Japanese, supplementary Unicode, 255 and 1024 character strings and long layer names are retained in JWW.",
    "Native DXF export of the unicode case exited before writing ENDSEC/EOF, while exporting its 1024-character text. Unicode native DXF export is not qualified; JWW-only save/reopen succeeds.",
    "The basic native DXF uses A3 center offset (210,148.5). The settings export uses a common scale factor 0.5 and A4 offset (148.5,105). These are measured export settings, not a general model-coordinate conversion rule.",
    "Native geometry/base attributes and all exposed layer settings are compared in Rust; native DXF geometry/text tags are checked independently."
  ],
